@tradition film-night
// W3 rec deck words. Saturdays 20:00-22:15, the junior common room; from the first Saturday after the first all-hands, the auditorium (lead 17's call 1: it moves once ship-wide events exist). RA: the existing hand-written film tradition's words; use whichever block matches where it is.
== mail
- Film night tomorrow, {time} in the junior common room. Bring a cushion. Somebody always cries.
== mail.auditorium
- Film night tomorrow, {time} in the auditorium. The screen comes down, the lights go down, and there's popcorn from the galley.
== ask
- Film tonight. I'm sitting at the back. I always fall asleep in the good bit.   #funny
- Are you coming to film night? Bring a cushion, or come early for the good seats.
== here
- Shh, it's starting.
- Pass the popcorn. Please. Thank you.
== thanks
- You find a seat as the lights go down. The film starts with a long shot of a lighthouse. Somebody sighs happily.   #warm
== chatter
- What's on at film night? Nobody ever knows till it starts.
- I cried at the film. It was the lighthouse. It's always the lighthouse.   #funny
